WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:04.640
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute Papers
with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:09.380
The research field of image translation with
the aid of learning algorithms has been on

00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:10.800
fire lately.

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:15.400
For instance, this earlier technique would
look at a large number of animal faces, and

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:21.390
could interpolate between them, or in other
words, blend one kind of dog into another

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:22.390
breed.

00:00:22.390 --> 00:00:27.390
But that’s not all, because it could even
transform dogs into cats, or create these

00:00:27.390 --> 00:00:29.869
glorious plump cats and cheetahs.

00:00:29.869 --> 00:00:36.060
The results were absolutely stunning, however,
it would only work on the domains it was trained

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:37.060
on.

00:00:37.060 --> 00:00:41.560
In other words, it could only translate to
and from species that it took the time to

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:42.560
learn about.

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:49.120
This new method offers something really amazing:
it can handle multiple domains, or multiple

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:53.700
breeds, if you will, even ones that it hadn’t
seen previously.

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:58.050
That sounds flat out impossible, so let’s
have a look at some results.

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:03.731
This dog will be used as content, therefore
the output should have a similar pose, but

00:01:03.731 --> 00:01:06.710
its breed has to be changed to this one.

00:01:06.710 --> 00:01:09.360
But there is one little problem.

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:13.550
And that problem is that the AI has never
seen this breed before.

00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:18.940
This will be very challenging because we only
see the head of the dog used for style.

00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:21.800
Should the body of the dog also get curly
hair?

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:27.160
You only know if you know this particular
dog breed, or if you are smart and can infer

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:30.640
missing information by looking at other kinds
of dogs.

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:33.080
Let’s see the result.

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:34.740
Incredible.

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:38.970
The remnants of the leash also remain there
in the output results.

00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:45.430
It also did a nearly impeccable job with this
bird, where again, the style image is from

00:01:45.430 --> 00:01:47.420
a previously unseen breed.

00:01:47.420 --> 00:01:52.820
Now, this is, of course, a remarkably difficult
problem domain, translating into different

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:58.220
kinds of animals that you know nothing about
apart from a tiny, cropped image, this would

00:01:58.220 --> 00:02:01.350
be quite a challenge, even for a human.

00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:06.140
However, this one is not the first technique
to attempt to solve it, so let’s see how

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:08.810
it stacks up against a previous method.

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:13.410
This one is from just a year ago, and you
will see in a moment how much this field has

00:02:13.410 --> 00:02:15.090
progressed since then.

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:20.610
For instance, in this output, we get two dogs,
which seems to be a mix of the content and

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:21.830
the style dog.

00:02:21.830 --> 00:02:26.819
And, while the new method still seems to have
some structural issues, the dog type and the

00:02:26.819 --> 00:02:29.069
pose is indeed correct.

00:02:29.069 --> 00:02:32.760
The rest of the results also appear to be
significantly better.

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:34.000
But what do you think?

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:35.569
Did you notice something weird?

00:02:35.569 --> 00:02:37.650
Let me know in the comments below.

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:41.240
And now, let’s transition into image interpolation.

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:45.240
This will be a touch more involved than previous
interpolation efforts.

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:50.420
You see, in this previous paper, we had a
source and a target image, and the AI was

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:53.930
asked to generate intermediate images between
them.

00:02:53.930 --> 00:02:55.390
Simple enough.

00:02:55.390 --> 00:03:00.160
In this case, however, we have not two, but
three images as an input.

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:05.111
There will be a content image, this will provide
the high-level features, such as pose, and

00:03:05.111 --> 00:03:08.970
its style is going to transition from this
to this.

00:03:08.970 --> 00:03:14.739
The goal is that the content image remains
intact while transforming one breed or species

00:03:14.739 --> 00:03:19.830
into another.

00:03:19.830 --> 00:03:22.760
This particular example is one of my favorites.

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:28.110
Such a beautiful transition, and surely not
all, but many of the intermediate images could

00:03:28.110 --> 00:03:29.680
stand on their own.

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:33.560
Again, the style images are from unseen species.

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:37.810
Not all cases do this well with the intermediate
images, however.

00:03:37.810 --> 00:03:43.060
We start with one eye because the content
and this style image have one eye visible,

00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:46.900
while the target style of the owl has two.

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:48.360
How do we solve that?

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:52.150
Of course, with nuclear fission.

00:03:52.150 --> 00:03:54.760
Look!

00:03:54.760 --> 00:03:55.760
Very amusing.

00:03:55.760 --> 00:04:00.989
Loving this example, especially how impossible
it seems because the owl is looking into the

00:04:00.989 --> 00:04:06.420
camera with both eyes, while, we see its backside
below the head.

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:11.660
If it looked to the side, like the input content
image, this might be a possibility, but with

00:04:11.660 --> 00:04:16.950
this contorted body posture, I am not so sure,
so I’ll give it a pass on this one.

00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:22.460
So there you go, transforming one known animal
into a different one that the AI has never

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:23.779
seen before.

00:04:23.779 --> 00:04:27.610
And it is already doing a more than formidable
job at that.

00:04:27.610 --> 00:05:13.619
What a time to 
be alive!

00:05:13.619 --> 00:05:22.569
Thanks for watching and for your generous
support, and I'll see you next time!

